AddReactionToAnItemResponse.description:
Slack Web API reactions.add response.

Typical success: {"ok": true}
Typical error: {"ok": false, "error": "<code>"}, possibly including scope diagnostics.

ConvertChannelToPrivateResponse.description:
Complete response for admin.conversations.convertToPrivate.

Matches Slack's documented response schema:
  - Success: { ok: true, warning?, response_metadata? }
  - Error:   { ok: false, error, needed?, provided?, warning?, response_metadata? }

DeleteChannelResponse.description:
Complete response for admin.conversations.delete.

Matches Slack's documented oneOf schema:
  - Success: { ok: true, warning?, response_metadata? }
  - Error:   { ok: false, error, needed?, provided?, warning?, response_metadata? }

DeletesAMessageFromAChatResponse.description:
Slack chat.delete response schema. Returns a flat object with success or error details.

Matches Slack docs: on success -> {"ok": true, "channel": "C123ABC456", "ts": "1401383885.000061"}
On error -> {"ok": false, "error": "message_not_found"}
Also accommodates optional top-level warning and response_metadata fields Slack may include.

GetReminderResponse.description:
Slack Web API reminders.info response schema.

- Success: {"ok": true, "reminder": Reminder}
- Error: {"ok": false, "error": "..."}

InviteUserToChannelResponse.description:
Response schema for `InviteUserToChannel` aligned with Slack conversations.invite API.

Success: { ok: true, channel: {...} }
Error: { ok: false, error: string }
Partial failures: { ok: true, channel: {...}, errors: [{user, ok, error}, ...] }

JoinAnExistingConversationResponse.description:
Slack Web API conversations.join response schema.

On success: { ok: true, channel: ChannelObject, warning?, response_metadata? }
On error:   { ok: false, error: string, needed?, provided? }
